# Copy this file to .env for local development.
#
# 1) Anthropic key — SERVER-SIDE ONLY (no VITE_ prefix), so it never ships to the browser.
#    The Express server (server.js) and its /api/claude proxy read this.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_key_here

# 2) Postgres (Render). Connection string from your Render Postgres dashboard
#    ("External Database URL"). Leave blank for quick local use (per-browser email+password,
#    no accounts). Render requires SSL; if you point at a LOCAL Postgres, set PGSSL=off.
DATABASE_URL=
# PGSSL=off                          # uncomment only for a local non-SSL Postgres

# 3) Auth — the secret used to sign/verify login JWTs. Generate a long random string:
#    node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
#    Required for real accounts; must be the SAME value everywhere the server runs.
AUTH_JWT_SECRET=
# JWT_ISS=karma-connect              # optional; issuer stamped into tokens (default shown)

# 4) Email — via the internal mail gateway. OPTIONAL, but sign-up confirmation
#    and password RESET do not work without it.
#
#    This app holds no mail-provider key. It POSTs to ${GATEWAY_URL}/send with
#    its own bearer token, and the gateway holds the provider credential and
#    decides which sender addresses that token may use. Ask an admin for a
#    token and to allowlist MAIL_FROM.
#
#    Unset: sending is off. Signups are created already-verified (convenient
#    for local dev) and "forgot password" reports that it cannot send, rather
#    than appearing to succeed.
GATEWAY_URL=                            # e.g. https://mailgate-xxxx.onrender.com
GATEWAY_TOKEN=                          # per-client bearer token (keep out of source control)
MAIL_FROM=Karma Connect <karmaconnect@karmastaff.com>   # must be allowlisted for this token
# APP_URL=https://karma-connect-9s2z.onrender.com        # base URL used in the email link;
#                                                          if unset, derived from the request

# --- Rate limiting + token quotas + response cache (optional but recommended for production) ---
# Create a free Upstash Redis DB -> copy the REST URL + token:
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://xxx.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...
# Tunables (optional, defaults shown):
# RATE_LIMIT_RPM=20                  # requests per user per minute
# DAILY_TOKEN_BUDGET=2000000         # tokens per user per day
# RESPONSE_CACHE_TTL=600             # seconds to cache identical requests
# BREAKER_FAILS=12                   # upstream failures/min before the global circuit breaker opens
# BREAKER_COOLDOWN=30                # seconds the breaker stays open
#
# Sign-up is OPEN by default: anyone who creates an account can use the app.
# To LOCK IT DOWN (recommended for a public URL — protects your API billing),
# set ONE of these on the server and only matching users are allowed:
# ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAIN=karmastaff.com               # only this email domain
# ALLOWED_EMAILS=a@karmastaff.com,b@karmastaff.com  # exact list (overrides the domain)

# Admins who can approve leads to unlock the Relationship / Meeting / Follow-up engines.
# Anyone NOT on this list is a normal member (free to use Hub + Intelligence + Connection,
# but the advanced engines stay locked per lead until an admin approves). Comma-separated.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=owner@karmastaff.com,manager@karmastaff.com

# The owner tier, above admin. An admin runs the day (approvals, engines, the
# team screen); an owner holds what changes who has access or cannot be undone
# — appointing admins, deleting accounts, emptying the Leads bin, lifting a
# do-not-call ban. Kept here rather than in the database on purpose: it has to
# survive a row being wrong, and it must not be grantable from inside the app.
# Defaults to tenzinwoesel@karmastaff.com when unset. Comma-separated.
# OWNER_EMAILS=tenzinwoesel@karmastaff.com
#
# (ADMIN_SIGNUP_CODE is gone. It was one shared string that made whoever typed
#  it an admin — unrevokable for a single person, and unlogged. The owner
#  grants admin from the Members screen now.)
#
# Local dev port for the backend (Vite proxies /api here). Render sets PORT itself.
# PORT=8787

# Where a click on a phone number sends the rep, when the in-page softphone
# is not available (a Zoho Telephony agent has no Zoho Voice web access, so
# the softphone cannot authenticate for them).
#
# Put {number} in it and the dialler opens ALREADY FILLED IN, which is the
# closest thing to pasting: a browser will not let one site type into
# another. The number is copied to the clipboard either way.
#
#   ZOHO_DIAL_URL=tel:{number}
#       ONLY if a desktop app on the rep's machine already registers itself
#       as the tel: handler AND that app is the one you want calls to go
#       through. Checked on a real machine here and Zoho was NOT among the
#       handlers offered — Windows listed Chrome, Edge, Skype, Teams and
#       Phone Link — so the click produced a chooser dialog and no call.
#       Zoho Voice has no desktop client that claims tel:, so on a Zoho-only
#       setup this is the wrong value: it brings back the app-chooser popup
#       for nothing.
#
#   ZOHO_DIAL_URL=https://<your dialler>/call?to={number}
#       Any dialler with a click-to-call URL. Ask whoever administers Zoho
#       what URL their CRM click-to-call uses and copy it here.
#
# WITHOUT {number} the page opens and the rep pastes (Ctrl+V). Left unset,
# or after the softphone has been refused, nothing opens at all and the
# number is simply copied — better than a tab reading "Access Denied", and
# better than a chooser dialog listing apps that cannot place the call.
# UNSET IS THE RIGHT DEFAULT until you have a URL that is known to reach
# the dialler your reps actually use.
# ZOHO_DIAL_URL=tel:{number}
#
# Prospect research scrapes LinkedIn through Apify rather than searching the
# open web — this server runs on Render, and LinkedIn shows a datacenter IP a
# login wall. Needs APIFY_TOKEN (above) plus an actor id from the Apify store.
# Not defaulted on purpose: LinkedIn actors change id and return different
# shapes, and a wrong default would fail as a 404 nobody can read. Without
# these, research falls back to the web search it used before.
# APIFY_LINKEDIN_COMPANY_ACTOR=<owner~actor-name>
# APIFY_LINKEDIN_PROFILE_ACTOR=<owner~actor-name>   # optional; company actor is used if unset
#
# The 7am storm digest. Triggered from OUTSIDE the app
# (.github/workflows/daily-digest.yml), because a free Render instance sleeps
# after ~15 min and an in-process timer is not awake at 7am to fire anything.
# The same knock also flushes any follow-back reminders that came due
# overnight, so this is worth having even if the digest is switched off.
#   CRON_TOKEN   shared secret; the endpoint refuses everything without it,
#                and refuses everything when it is unset. Put the same value
#                in the repo's Actions secrets.
#   DIGEST_TZ    the team's timezone; the schedule fires twice in UTC and the
#                server picks the run that is actually 7am local, so the
#                digest survives daylight saving without editing a cron line.
# CRON_TOKEN=<a long random string>
# DIGEST_TZ=America/New_York
# DIGEST_HOUR=7
# DIGEST_LAST_HOUR=16   # GitHub fires schedules late; any knock 7..16 local sends
#
# ─────────────────────── Karma Leads (served at /leads) ───────────────────────
# Karma Connect and Karma Leads run as ONE service. Leads keeps its own database
# and its own WorkOS sign-in; nothing is shared but the process and the hostname.
#
# Leads' Postgres — the existing karma-db. Deliberately a SEPARATE variable from
# DATABASE_URL above so the two apps can never end up pointed at one database.
# Leave blank locally: Leads simply won't mount, and Connect runs as normal.
LEADS_DATABASE_URL=
#
# WorkOS AuthKit — Leads' sign-in. All four must be set or nobody can log in
# (the server warns loudly at boot when they're incomplete). WORKOS_REDIRECT_URI
# must be <this host>/api/auth/callback AND be allowlisted in the WorkOS
# dashboard under Redirects — the host changed when the apps merged.
WORKOS_API_KEY=
WORKOS_CLIENT_ID=
WORKOS_REDIRECT_URI=
SESSION_SECRET=                        # seals the kl_session cookie
#
# APIFY_TOKEN=                         # admin "Find jobs"; blank disables job search
# AUTO_INVITE_DOMAIN=karmastaff.com    # auto-enrol this domain as members ("" to disable)
# LEADS_APP_PATH=/leads/               # where sign-in returns to (derived automatically)
# LEADS_ENABLED=0                      # unmount Karma Leads without a code change

# ── DEV ONLY: sign-in bypass ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Treats every local request as this person, so both products can be used
# without a WorkOS round trip. Three independent guards keep it out of
# production: NODE_ENV must not be "production" (Render's blueprint sets
# exactly that), this variable must be set deliberately, and the request must
# come from loopback. Leave blank to require real sign-in.
# DEV_AUTH_EMAIL=you@karmastaff.com

# ── DEV ONLY: demo data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Serves the assignments board (and the KPI row) from an invented team and
# invented leads held in memory, so the screen can be used without a database.
# Assigning really works against that in-memory set. Guarded the same way as
# DEV_AUTH_EMAIL: ignored unless NODE_ENV is not "production", and never
# mounted at all otherwise. Everything it returns is flagged demo:true and the
# board shows a banner. Never set this on a deploy.
# KARMA_DEMO=1
# DEV_AUTH_ROLE=member          # with the bypass on, see the salesperson's view

# ── The dialler: RingCentral (per rep) ────────────────────────────────────────
# These two decide whether the soft dialler exists AT ALL. The server computes
#   ENABLED = !!(RINGCENTRAL_CLIENT_ID && RINGCENTRAL_CLIENT_SECRET)
# and when it is false /api/voice/rc/status answers {enabled:false}, no phone
# ever registers, the launcher never appears, and every rep silently falls
# back to Zoho. If the dialler is "missing" on a machine, check these first:
# a seat connected in the database is NOT enough on its own.
#
# They are per DEPLOYMENT, not per rep — each rep then signs in once through
# /api/voice/rc/connect and their own refresh token is stored against their
# user. Get the pair from the app at https://developers.ringcentral.com
# (Credentials tab). The app needs the "VoIP Calling" permission or the SIP
# provision call returns 403.
#
# RINGCENTRAL_CLIENT_ID=
# RINGCENTRAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# RINGCENTRAL_SERVER_URL=https://platform.ringcentral.com
#                    # the sandbox is https://platform.devtest.ringcentral.com
#                    # — it only reaches RingCentral's own test numbers, and
#                    # the app says so in a banner when it detects devtest.
# APP_URL=http://localhost:8787   # where RingCentral sends the rep back after
#                    # they authorise. Must match the app's redirect URI.

# ── Click-to-call: Zoho Voice (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# ZOHO_DIAL_MODE picks what clicking a phone number does. None of these change
# what Zoho charges — the subscription and the per-minute call credits are the
# same either way. They differ only in how much of the dialling happens inside
# Karma Leads.
#
#   tel  (default)  Leave it a plain tel: link. Zoho ZDialer (the browser
#                   extension) and the Zoho Voice desktop app both answer tel:,
#                   so this is click-to-call with NO integration at all.
#                   Try this one first — it may be all you need.
#   web             Copy the number and open the Zoho dialler in a reused tab.
#                   No credentials needed. One paste per call, unless
#                   ZOHO_DIAL_URL carries a {number} placeholder to prefill it.
#   sdk             In-page softphone via the Zoho WebSDK. Best experience,
#                   needs the OAuth credentials below, and falls back to tel:
#                   when they are missing.
#
# ZOHO_DIAL_MODE=tel
# ZOHO_DIAL_URL=https://voice.zoho.com
#   If Zoho documents a prefill parameter for your account, put {number} where
#   the digits belong, e.g. https://voice.zoho.com/somepath?number={number}
#
# The rest is only read when ZOHO_DIAL_MODE=sdk. Phone numbers stay plain tel:
# links without it — the integration is an upgrade, never a dependency.
#
# The refresh token is exchanged for short-lived access tokens SERVER-SIDE
# (server/voice.js) and never reaches the browser.
# ZOHO_VOICE_ENABLED=1
# ZOHO_CLIENT_ID=
# ZOHO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# ZOHO_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# ZOHO_ACCOUNTS_DOMAIN=https://accounts.zoho.com   # .eu / .in / .com.au as applicable

# KARMA_NO_SWEEP=1   # dev only: connect to a real database WITHOUT running the
#                    # 30-day trash purge, which permanently deletes binned leads
